! Oracle anchor, v1.21.0.  MP2 against ORCA 6.0.1 at the exact
! geometry the reference used.
!
! ONE NON-DEFAULT KEY: %pump2 no.
!
! StudDFT reports the SPIN-PROJECTED energy by default when UMP2
! is active; ORCA reports UMP2.  On CH3 the two differ by 2.8 mHa,
! which is the size of the projection and not of any disagreement.
! With %pump2 no they agree to 6e-9 Ha.  This is not an accuracy
! setting -- without it the test compares two different quantities
! and calls the difference an error.
!
! FROZEN CORE IS LEFT AT THE DEFAULT, and BeH2 and NaCl are absent
! from the MP2 anchors because of it.  The two programs use
! different core definitions: StudDFT freezes the noble-gas core,
! ORCA uses its own per-element table which correlates all
! electrons of Be and treats Na differently.  Forcing
! %frozen_core 0 fixes those two and breaks the other nineteen --
! MAD went from 0.02 to 1449 uHa.  Neither convention is wrong;
! they are simply not the same, and the paper lists exactly these
! two molecules as the MP2 maxima for the same reason.
!
%method  MP2
%basis   cc-pVDZ
%job     energy
%charge  0
%mult    1
%spherical
%pump2 no
%scf_etol 1e-10
%scf_ptol 1e-8
%scf_diis_etol 1e-7
%geom angstrom
H  0. 0. 0.
F  0. 0. 0.92
*end
